1e:T54f,G42 is an Abu Dhabi-based company founded in 2018; the supplied seed identifies Sheikh Tahnoun bin Zayed as chair and Peng Xiao as CEO, and names Mubadala, Microsoft, and Silver Lake among its owners . Its group includes Core42, formed to deliver national-scale enterprise AI solutions and services, including cloud, AI and HPC infrastructure, applied AI, cybersecurity, and professional services . G42â€™s portfolio company Inception developed (In)Business Procurement, which G42 said can reduce sourcing and contract cycles by up to 40% . Core42 announced a 42MW expansion at its Lake Mariner site in New York, increasing site capacity from 18MW to 60MW; separately, a July 2026 report said G42 joined Nvidiaâ€™s Open Secure AI Alliance . Bloomberg was identified in the seed as reporting in September 2026 that G42 was exploring a multibillion-dollar raise and a possible US majority stake . Ownership (verified 21 Oct 2026): Sheikh Tahnoon bin Zayed Al Nahyan is chairman and controlling shareholder; Mubadala, Microsoft (US$1.5B, Apr 2024, board seat Brad Smith), Silver Lake and the Dalio Family Office hold minority stakes; exact percentages unavailable . Bloomberg's Sep 2026 raise/majority-stake reports remain reported, unconfirmed . G42 welcomed US approval for advanced AI chip exports (~20 Oct 2026) and announced an Assurance Compute Framework .1f:T410,Inception (Inception42) is G42's AI product company, headquartered in Abu Dhabi. Ashish Koshy has been CEO since June 2025 (WAM 4 May 2026; Entrepreneur ME 22 Feb 2026); Dr Andrew Jackson transitioned to G42 Group Chief AI Officer around June 2025 . G42 describes Inception as a portfolio company and announced its (In)Business Procurement platform, which is intended to reduce sourcing and contract cycles by up to 40% . G42 also reported that Inception was among the businesses brought together to form Core42, so the available evidence does not establish Inceptionâ€™s current standalone legal or operating structure . Inceptionâ€™s Maria Sanchez described a deployment at an unnamed fund during a 2026 panel, and Jais 3 was released with MBZUAIâ€™s Institute of Foundation Models on 2026-10-15 . Jais 3 (15 Oct 2026, with MBZUAI's IFM) comprises six open models from 0.9B to 375B parameters plus Jais Speech covering the dialects of 19 Arab countries, with a 512K context window, built on IFM's fully open K2 Horizon fleet (Sept 2026) .20:T4c5,AIREV is an Abu Dhabi company founded in September 2023 by Muhammad Khalid (Founder & CEO), Kayaan Unwalla and Dr Youssef Youssef (Co-Founder & COO) ; it entered the UAE through NextGenFDI anchored by Core42 (a G42 company) in February 2024 and launched its agentic-AI platform OnDemand with Core42 in July 2024 . H.E. Dr Thani bin Ahmed Al Zeyoudi, Minister of Foreign Trade, was named Chairman in June 2026 . Reported investors are Core42, VentureWave Capital (Apr 2025) and Titian Capital, with a reported ~US$200M valuation and a Series A2 in progress (reported, unconfirmed) . Partnerships: Tenstorrent (25 Jun 2025), Intel MoU at GITEX GLOBAL 2025 (14 Oct 2025) and on-device AI-PC agents (Dec 2025), Supermicro 'Certified by AIREV' (Oct 2025), Redington GCC+Africa distribution (22 Jul 2026) and Qualcomm Dragonwing (13 Aug 2026) ; OnDemand is listed on AWS Marketplace and the Cisco AI ISV Showcase . Company-reported metrics (not independently verified): 4M+ users, 300+ agents, 50+ languages, 6.8T tokens processed in Q2 2026. SOC 2 Type I/II and ISO claims appear only on AIREV's LinkedIn and are marked self-reported, unverified. Rani Plaut and airev.aero refer to a different entity (eVTOL) and are excluded.e:["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","header",null,{"className":"mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-end justify-between gap-4 py-2","data-testid":"section-header","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-2xl","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-[#737373]","children":"Watchlist"}],["$","h1",null,{"className":"text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#0D0D0D] sm:text-[28px]","children":"50 organisations shaping UAE AI"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-2 text-sm text-[#5D5D5D] sm:text-[15px]","children":"Companies, government bodies, universities, research centres and subsidiaries. Mean research coverage 73% Â· 36 high-confidence dossiers Â· parents and subsidiaries are de-duplicated into 34 ecosystem groups for aggregates."}]]}],"$undefined"]}],["$","$L1d",null,{"cards":[{"id":"ai-data-authority","name":"Artificial Intelligence and Data Authority","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["National artificial intelligence","Government data and data integration","Digital government","AI strategy and governance","Driving AI's contribution to UAE GDP"],"confidence":0.91,"coverage":0.909,"news":4,"voices":10,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"On 14 June 2026, Sheikh Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum approved the Authority's establishment as the single national body responsible for data, artificial intelligence and digital government, reporting directly to the Cabinet . The Authority brings together the AI Office and UAE Data Office and incorporates the digital government portfolio of the Telecommunications and Digital Government Regulatory Authority . H.E. Omar Sultan Al Olama was named to lead the Authority; he was first appointed Minister of State for Artificial Intelligence in October 2017, with his portfolio expanded in July 2020 . Its stated remit includes national AI strategy, digital government services, government data integration and increasing AI's direct contribution to UAE GDP .","root":"ai-data-authority"},{"id":"g42","name":"G42","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Artificial intelligence","Cloud computing and high-performance computing","National-scale enterprise AI solutions","Applied AI and generative AI for enterprise use cases","AI infrastructure","AI-enabled procurement optimization","Open and secure AI"],"confidence":0.79,"coverage":1,"news":29,"voices":50,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"$1e","root":"g42"},{"id":"core42","name":"Core42","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"G42","focus":["National-scale enterprise AI solutions and services","Sovereign cloud and AI infrastructure","High-performance computing for public-sector and regulated-industry workloads","Applied AI research and enterprise generative AI","Cybersecurity and technology services"],"confidence":0.88,"coverage":1,"news":8,"voices":8,"models":0,"unavailable":3,"summary":"Core42 is an Abu Dhabi-based G42 subsidiary formed in October 2023 by combining G42 Cloud, Injazat, and Inception.  Its remit includes enterprise AI, sovereign cloud, AI and HPC infrastructure, and applied AI; the 2026 U.S. deployment announcement identifies Talal M. Al Kaissi as CEO, while the formation announcement named Kiril Evtimov to lead the company.  Core42 announced a 42MW expansion at Lake Mariner in New York, taking that site's capacity from 18MW to 60MW; the announcement also describes U.S. deployments and European expansion.  Seed facts report $550 million in financing in May 2026, while supplied reporting describes its e& UAE sovereign-compute partnership and contribution to the DoHâ€“Johnson & Johnson surgical network.","root":"g42"},{"id":"inception","name":"Inception (Inception42, G42)","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"G42","focus":["AI product development","Enterprise AI and workflow augmentation","Arabic-language foundation models through collaboration with MBZUAIâ€™s Institute of Foundation Models"],"confidence":0.79,"coverage":0.864,"news":6,"voices":4,"models":8,"unavailable":5,"summary":"$1f","root":"g42"},{"id":"presight","name":"Presight AI Holding PLC","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"G42","focus":["Cross-sector big data analytics","AI-powered solutions","Product development"],"confidence":0.88,"coverage":0.909,"news":4,"voices":2,"models":0,"unavailable":3,"summary":"Presight AI Holding PLC is an Abu Dhabi-headquartered, ADX-listed company and part of the G42 ecosystem; the cited ownership breakdown gives G42 70.5%, ITG 15%, ADNOC 4%, and free float 10.5%.  Thomas Pramotedham is CEO and Mansoor Al Mansoori is Chairman.  Presightâ€™s stated capabilities include cross-sector big data analytics and product development, and its announced AIQ restructuring would make it the 51% shareholder alongside ADNOC at 49%, subject to approvals.  AIQ, described as a Presight company, announced a $340 million contract with ADNOC to deploy ENERGYai and related AI solutions across upstream operations.","root":"g42"},{"id":"aiq","name":"AIQ","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"Presight AI Holding PLC","focus":["Developing and commercializing AI products and applications for the oil and gas industry.","Applying AI to energy operations, including ADNOC upstream workflows.","Using agentic AI and large language models to support analysis, modeling, and process monitoring."],"confidence":0.88,"coverage":1,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":3,"summary":"AIQ is an Abu Dhabi-based energy AI company launched by ADNOC and G42, and its ownership structure is Presight 51% and ADNOC 49%; the earlier joint venture was held 60% by ADNOC and 40% by G42.  AIQâ€™s stated focus is developing and commercializing AI products for oil and gas, and it remains a standalone company within Presightâ€™s portfolio.  AIQ announced a $340 million, three-year ADNOC contract to deploy ENERGYai and associated AI solutions across ADNOCâ€™s upstream value chain.  ENERGYai combines large language models with agentic AI trained for specific workflows, including seismic analysis, geological modeling, and real-time process monitoring.","root":"g42"},{"id":"khazna","name":"Khazna Data Centers","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"G42","focus":["Physical data-center infrastructure supporting AI compute","Stargate UAE infrastructure","Data-center capacity for the Microsoft-G42 partnership"],"confidence":0.78,"coverage":0.818,"news":11,"voices":15,"models":0,"unavailable":7,"summary":"Khazna is an Abu Dhabi-based data-center subsidiary with Hassan Alnaqbi identified as CEO in the supplied seed facts; no source URL or date was provided for those details. G42 is identified as the majority owner, while e& sold its 40% stake in 2025 to G42, Silver Lake, and MGX; the current individual percentages are not specified. Khaznaâ€™s 200 MW Stargate UAE phase-1 enclosures were reported complete in August 2026, with two 100 MW buildings making up the phase. The supplied reporting describes Khazna as the physical infrastructure builder for Stargate UAE, while G42 leads the project and OpenAI and Oracle operate it. A separate 200 MW data-center expansion through Khazna was announced by Microsoft and G42.","root":"g42"},{"id":"m42","name":"M42","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"G42","focus":["Healthcare AI and clinical care","Health data exchange and integrated health data","AI-assisted diagnostics","Chronic disease care and population health","Precision medicine and clinical research","Using AI to predict conditions and improve medical outcomes"],"confidence":0.83,"coverage":0.818,"news":9,"voices":8,"models":0,"unavailable":3,"summary":"M42 was formed through the transfer of Mubadala Health and a joint venture with G42, with ownership stated as G42 55% and Mubadala 45% . Its Digital Health Solutions platform includes Abu Dhabi Health Data Services, which connects healthcare systems and supports health data exchange . In June 2026, M42â€™s National Reference Laboratory worked with Qritive on AI-based prostate cancer diagnostics, with doctors retaining final clinical authority . M42 announced plans in September 2026 to adopt Oracle Health Data Intelligence with Oracle Health Foundation EHR to unify clinical, genomic, and real-world data . Dimitris Moulavasilis is identified as M42â€™s chief executive, and the mission brief gives his Group CEO start as May 2025 .","root":"g42"},{"id":"space42","name":"Space42 PLC","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["AI-powered space technology","Earth observation","Geospatial intelligence"],"confidence":0.88,"coverage":0.909,"news":2,"voices":5,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Space42 is an Abu Dhabi-headquartered, ADX-listed company formed through the Bayanatâ€“Yahsat merger, which became effective on 1 October 2024; the reported post-merger shareholder split was 54% for Bayanat shareholders and 46% for Yahsat shareholders.  The verified seed facts identify Karim Michel Sabbagh as Managing Director and report H1 2026 revenue of $260 million, up 15%, with a $6.3 billion backlog.  Space42 announced on 9 June 2026 that Foresight-3, Foresight-4, and Foresight-5 were operational, expanding its Foresight Earth Observation constellation to five SAR satellites.  The company said the three satellites were manufactured with ICEYE in Finland, with critical integration and testing completed at its Abu Dhabi facility.","root":"space42"},{"id":"mgx","name":"MGX","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Investment in artificial intelligence technologies","AI infrastructure and data-centre investment"],"confidence":0.74,"coverage":0.818,"news":1,"voices":1,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"MGX is an Abu Dhabi AI investment company established in 2024 by G42 and Mubadala.  One source describes an MGX target of USD 25 billion, while another reports plans to deploy up to USD 10 billion annually; these are differently framed figures.  In 2025, MGX joined an AI Infrastructure Partnership targeting data centres and energy solutions, with potential investment of up to USD 100 billion.  On 2026-09-25, an MGX-backed consortium was reported to be discussing a data-centre portfolio across Tokyo, Sydney, and Johor Bahru.","root":"mgx"},{"id":"analog","name":"Analog","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"G42","focus":["Spatial AI computing","Enterprise AI","Applied AI products"],"confidence":0.65,"coverage":0.636,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":7,"summary":"The supplied mission brief describes Analog as a spatial/AI computing company of G42 led by Alex Kipman . Research material describes Analog as a G42-owned business in enterprise AI and applied products, within the G42 ecosystem . The available research does not disclose Analogâ€™s specific shareholding .","root":"g42"},{"id":"tii","name":"Technology Innovation Institute","type":"research centre","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"Advanced Technology Research Council","focus":["Artificial intelligence and foundation models","Multimodal vision-language systems","Arabic-language AI, including Emirati Arabic","Speech recognition and Arabic document processing","Quantum computing","Autonomous robotics","Cryptography and secure systems","Advanced materials and digital science","Directed energy"],"confidence":0.82,"coverage":0.909,"news":7,"voices":14,"models":68,"unavailable":2,"summary":"TII is an Abu Dhabi research centre and the applied research pillar of ATRC, with a focus spanning AI and other advanced-technology fields.  Its Falcon portfolio includes foundation, reasoning, Arabic-language, multimodal, and document-focused models; TII launched Falcon Perception in May 2026.  Dr. Najwa Aaraj has been CEO since 21 May 2024, succeeding inaugural CEO Dr Ray O. Johnson (2021â€“2024) .  A reported AWS collaboration made a selection of Falcon models available through Amazon Bedrock Marketplace, expanding their global reach.","root":"atrc"},{"id":"atrc","name":"Advanced Technology Research Council","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Research policy","Strategic research and advanced technology","Artificial intelligence","Government AI ecosystem"],"confidence":0.83,"coverage":0.909,"news":3,"voices":7,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"ATRC is an Abu Dhabi government research-policy body and the parent of TII, AI71, and ASPIRE . Faisal Al Bannai is ATRCâ€™s Secretary-General; Reuters also identifies him as an adviser to the UAE President on strategic research and advanced technology . TII is described as ATRCâ€™s applied research pillar, and its work includes the Falcon model family . TII and AI71 have been described as part of ATRCâ€™s ecosystem and as collaborating with AWS to expand access to UAE-developed AI models and products .","root":"atrc"},{"id":"ai71","name":"AI71","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"Advanced Technology Research Council","focus":["Commercialisation of Falcon","Enterprise AI products"],"confidence":0.68,"coverage":0.727,"news":1,"voices":1,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"AI71 is an Abu Dhabi-based subsidiary and AI company associated with ATRC . The mission brief identifies Dr Mahir Nayfeh as CEO and says AI71 commercialises Falcon . AI71 and TII signed a collaboration with AWS to expand access to UAE-made AI models and associated enterprise AI products through Amazon Bedrock Marketplace .","root":"atrc"},{"id":"edge","name":"EDGE Group","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Group AI Accelerator for advancing AI development and integration across defence solutions and manufacturing","Autonomous air and land systems","AI-enabled defence systems and platforms"],"confidence":0.83,"coverage":0.818,"news":3,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"EDGE Group is an Abu Dhabi-headquartered defence and advanced-technology company; the supplied seed identifies Hamad Al Marar as CEO and Faisal Al Bannai as chair.  Its Group AI Accelerator is described as a Centre of Excellence intended to advance AI in defence solutions and manufacturing and develop local talent.  EDGEâ€™s autonomous-systems activity includes the REACH-S UAV, with ADASI identified as an EDGE entity responsible for production and delivery.  The Omen autonomous air vehicle was developed under the EDGE-Anduril Production Alliance and is reported to run on Andurilâ€™s Lattice AI software.  EDGEâ€™s international plans include a Paris office in June 2026 and a scheduled ADEX 2026 appearance in Baku.","root":"edge"},{"id":"katim","name":"KATIM","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"EDGE Group","focus":[],"confidence":0.3,"coverage":0.273,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":9,"summary":"KATIM is identified in the mission brief as an EDGE Group secure communications and cyber entity . Its headquarters is Abu Dhabi, as specified in the brief . No details are provided about KATIMâ€™s AI programs, products, leadership, founding date, ownership terms, or international expansion .","root":"edge"},{"id":"adasi","name":"ADASI","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"EDGE Group","focus":["Acquires, operates, customises, and maintains autonomous systems across air, land, and sea","Designs and develops autonomous systems"],"confidence":0.84,"coverage":0.909,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":3,"summary":"ADASI is an EDGE Group entity focused on autonomous systems, with capabilities spanning acquisition, operation, customisation, and maintenance across air, land, and sea.  It also designs and develops autonomous systems; for the REACH-S contract, ADVANCED CONCEPTS developed the aircraft while ADASI was assigned production oversight and delivery to the UAE Armed Forces.  EDGE showcased ADASIâ€™s QX UAVs, SCORPIO UGVs, and GARMOOSHA unmanned aircraft at UMEX 2022.  Reuters reported that ADASI clinched a 1.33 billion-dirham deal for its Shadow system in February 2023.","root":"edge"},{"id":"mbzuai","name":"Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence","type":"university","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Artificial intelligence research and education","Foundation models","Advanced AI reasoning","Arabic-native language models and speech recognition"],"confidence":0.86,"coverage":0.818,"news":8,"voices":17,"models":64,"unavailable":5,"summary":"MBZUAI is a public university in Abu Dhabiâ€™s Masdar City community; it received a UAE Ministry of Education license in April 2020, began graduate programs in January 2021, and launched an undergraduate program in 2025.  Its model work includes K2 Think, launched with G42 in September 2025, and K2 Horizon, released on 2026-09-03 as a suite of six fully open models.  MBZUAIâ€™s Institute of Foundation Models and Inception42 launched Jais 3, a set of open Arabic models with speech-recognition capability, built on K2 Horizon.  MBZUAI has also partnered with Abu Dhabiâ€™s Department of Health and Core42 on a Global AI Healthcare Academy.","root":"mbzuai"},{"id":"ifm","name":"Institute of Foundation Models (IFM), Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence","type":"research centre","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence","focus":["Foundation models","Open AI models and advanced reasoning","Arabic-native language and speech AI","AI agents"],"confidence":0.84,"coverage":0.818,"news":1,"voices":9,"models":14,"unavailable":3,"summary":"IFM is described as MBZUAIâ€™s internal research arm, with MBZUAI identified as its parent institution.  K2 Horizon is a suite of six fully open models ranging from 0.9B to 375B parameters, with weights, code, training data, and methods disclosed.  IFM and G42 announced K2 Think as an open-source system for advanced AI reasoning.  IFM and Inception42 launched Jais 3, a family built on K2 Horizon that includes Arabic models and speech recognition.","root":"mbzuai"},{"id":"khalifa-university","name":"Khalifa University of Science and Technology","type":"university","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":[],"confidence":0.35,"coverage":0.273,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":10,"summary":"Khalifa University of Science and Technology is a public research university.  It is based in Abu Dhabi.  The mission brief identifies its institutional type as a university.","root":"khalifa-university"},{"id":"airev","name":"AIREV","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Agentic AI","Autonomous AI platforms (OnDemand)","On-device AI agents (Intel Core Ultra AI PCs)","Sovereign / self-hosted agent deployments"],"confidence":0.86,"coverage":0.909,"news":6,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"$20","root":"airev"},{"id":"eand-enterprise","name":"e& enterprise","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["AI","Cloud","Cybersecurity","Enterprise AI applications and industry-specific use cases"],"confidence":0.78,"coverage":0.818,"news":1,"voices":2,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"e& enterprise is described as part of e& (formerly Etisalat Group) and as e&â€™s AI, cloud, and cybersecurity arm.  On 30 June 2022, it and Hub71 announced the launch of the regionâ€™s first AI Centre of Excellence in Abu Dhabi, offering a platform to build and scale AI solutions and support enterprise use cases.  The AI CoE was associated with a strategic alliance between e& enterprise and DataRobot, and its announcement named Salvador Anglada as e& enterpriseâ€™s CEO at that time.","root":"eand-enterprise"},{"id":"hub71","name":"Hub71","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Hub71+ AI specialist ecosystem","Supporting AI startups and enterprise AI applications","EchoTwin AI: digital twins and predictive maintenance for infrastructure","Neuphonic: efficient voice AI and real-time voice interactions","Endimension Technology: AI radiology, abnormality detection, triage and reporting","Harmonic Discovery: AI for precision-therapy design","Planys Technologies: autonomous underwater robots and smart sensors"],"confidence":0.82,"coverage":0.818,"news":2,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Hub71 describes itself as Abu Dhabiâ€™s global tech ecosystem and a community connecting innovators, corporate partners and investors.  Ahmad Ali Alwan is identified as Hub71â€™s CEO in reporting on Cohort 17.  Hub71â€™s Cohorts 17 and 18 included AI startups such as Harmonic Discovery, Planys Technologies, EchoTwin AI, Neuphonic and Endimension Technology.  Hub71 and e& enterprise announced an AI Centre of Excellence in Abu Dhabi in June 2022, and Hub71 has also established Hub71+ AI as a specialist ecosystem.","root":"hub71"},{"id":"micropolis","name":"Micropolis Robotics","type":"company","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Autonomous mobile robots and unmanned ground vehicles","Physical AI for perception, navigation, and fleet mission planning","Robotics for security, inspection, logistics, and smart infrastructure","Detection and behavioral intelligence"],"confidence":0.8,"coverage":1,"news":6,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Micropolis Robotics is a Dubai-based company founded in 2014 that develops autonomous mobile robots and Physical AI systems; the research describes a pivot into robotics and AI around 2018.  Its stated capabilities include perception, navigation, fleet mission planning, and systems for security, inspection, logistics, and other real-world operations.  The company is listed on NYSE American as MCRP, with trading reported to have begun on March 7, 2025.  The research identifies Dubai Police, ADNOC, and an Abu Dhabi autonomous sweeper deployment among its UAE relationships; the supplied seed also identifies EMSTEEL, but deal details for EMSTEEL are unavailable in the research snippets.","root":"micropolis"},{"id":"xpanceo","name":"XPANCEO","type":"company","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Smart contact lens technology combining optics, nanophotonics, materials science, biosensing, and AR/XR computing","AI systems for material discovery and prototyping workflows"],"confidence":0.84,"coverage":0.909,"news":4,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":2,"summary":"XPANCEO is a Dubai-based company founded in 2021, with its listed headquarters at Dubai Internet City, Emmay Tower.  Its leadership includes founder and CEO Roman Axelrod and CTO Dr. Valentyn S. Volkov.  The company focuses on smart contact lenses and related optics, nanophotonics, materials science, biosensing, AR/XR computing, and AI-assisted material discovery and prototyping.  In July 2025, it raised a $250 million Series A at a reported $1.35 billion valuation, with Opportunity Venture leading the round.","root":"xpanceo"},{"id":"derq","name":"Derq","type":"company","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Road-safety AI","Traffic accident prevention"],"confidence":0.72,"coverage":0.818,"news":1,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Derq is described as Dubai-based and focused on preventing road accidents through its patented DerqPrevent solution.  Derq signed an MoU with Smart Dubai Office, the Roads and Transport Authority, and Dubai Silicon Oasis Authority to implement its technology in Dubai.  The coverage states that DerqPrevent aims to predict 9 in 10 accidents before collision and warn drivers and vehicles.","root":"derq"},{"id":"astra-tech","name":"Astra Tech","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Consumer technology platform combining communications, fintech, and e-commerce, with AI-powered technology solutions.","The company describes using AI to enhance digital experiences; a specific AI product specialization is unavailable."],"confidence":0.79,"coverage":1,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Astra Tech is an Abu Dhabi-based company founded in 2022; its website describes it as the parent company of botim and presents the app as combining communications, fintech, e-commerce, and AI-powered solutions.  The companyâ€™s CEO is Tariq Bin Hendi, and Abdallah Abu Sheikh is identified as its founder and chairman.  The mission brief identifies a $500 million round led by G42; the available profile also describes a December 2024 investment in Quantix involving Citi and others, so the precise framing of the funding is not consistent across the supplied material.  Astra Techâ€™s website reports more than 150 million users across 155 countries.","root":"astra-tech"},{"id":"saal-ai","name":"Saal.ai","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Big data","Cognitive AI","AI agents","Natural language processing","Arabic-first cognitive AI solutions","Healthcare, defence, finance, and smart city applications"],"confidence":0.82,"coverage":0.818,"news":2,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"Saal.ai was founded in 2018 and is headquartered in Abu Dhabi, UAE.  CEO Vikraman Poduval leads a company focused on big data, cognitive AI, agents, and NLP, including Arabic-first solutions and applications across healthcare, defence, finance, and smart cities.  Its described offerings include an integrated big data platform, a platform for building AI agents, and Agentic AI products.  DXBStart lists a US$60 million Series A in June 2026, led by AI71 and BlueFive Capital.  In October 2026, Poduval spoke at AI Everything Abu Dhabi about showcasing the companyâ€™s big data and AI agent technologies.","root":"saal-ai"},{"id":"purehealth","name":"PureHealth","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Healthcare AI and diagnostic automation","AI-powered clinical documentation and digital health","AI-based health-insurance document processing"],"confidence":0.84,"coverage":0.727,"news":4,"voices":2,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"PureHealth is a healthcare group headquartered in Abu Dhabi, and the supplied research describes it as having a healthcare-focused AI laboratory . In December 2025, it launched an AI-powered diagnostic lab through PureLab, with automation, real-time quality control, robotics, and a network of more than 140 accredited laboratories . Its 2025 annual report describes Nada, an AI clinical assistant, and Pura, an AI-powered digital health companion . In September 2026, PureHealth announced AI document processing for Daman, reporting capacity above 60 million documents annually and service relevance to more than three million members .","root":"purehealth"},{"id":"daman","name":"Daman (The National Insurance Company)","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"PureHealth","focus":["Automating health-insurance document processing, including policy applications, endorsements, and claims","Converting insurance documents into structured data"],"confidence":0.78,"coverage":0.727,"news":0,"voices":2,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Daman is identified as a PureHealth subsidiary, and the company is based in Abu Dhabi . In September 2026, PureHealth announced an AI-powered solution for automating Damanâ€™s insurance document processing . The announced system is expected to process more than 60 million documents a year, convert over 80% into structured data, reduce processing from days to minutes, and cut manual rework by over 50% . Trade-media coverage describes processing for policy applications, endorsements, and claims using LLMs and document classification .","root":"purehealth"},{"id":"cntxt","name":"CNTXT AI","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Arabic-first AI models","Data and artificial intelligence","Training robots"],"confidence":0.55,"coverage":0.455,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":8,"summary":"CNTXT AI is described as a United Arab Emirates-based data and artificial-intelligence startup.  It has built Arabic-first AI models and is training robots.  The company raised $60 million in June, but the year is not specified in the available report excerpt.  It is expanding into Silicon Valley with an eye toward partnerships bridging the United States and the Middle East.","root":"cntxt"},{"id":"positron","name":"Positron AI Ltd","type":"company","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Inference hardware and infrastructure for power-efficient, scalable deployment of AI models"],"confidence":0.86,"coverage":0.636,"news":1,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"Positron AI Ltd is a US-based inference-hardware company, described as a unicorn.  Its focus is next-generation inference infrastructure for power-efficient, scalable deployment of AI models.  On 1 June 2026, it established its first presence outside the US in DIFC under the Dubai AI Licence.","root":"positron"},{"id":"cerebras-uae","name":"Cerebras Systems","type":"company","hq":"unavailable","parent":null,"focus":["AI computing and generative AI acceleration","Wafer-scale inference","High-speed inference and reasoning workloads"],"confidence":0.76,"coverage":0.545,"news":4,"voices":5,"models":0,"unavailable":7,"summary":"Gulf News reports that G42 and Cerebras co-developed a chip with 4 trillion transistors, showcased by Sheikh Saif at WGS 2026 . Core42â€™s U.S. deployments include Condor Galaxy supercomputers developed in collaboration with Cerebras, across sites including Buffalo, Dallas, Sunnyvale, Stockton, and Minneapolis . Khaleej Times reports that Core42 expected to deploy nearly 40,000 GPUs globally by year-end, supported by architectures including Cerebras systems . G42 said its technology collaborations with U.S. chipmakers include Cerebras, alongside projects such as Stargate UAE . The K2 Think announcement said the model would be available on Cerebrasâ€™ wafer-scale inference platform and described a planned throughput of 2,000 tokens per second using speculative decoding optimized for Cerebras hardware . Carnegie Endowment reported that G42, MBZUAI, and Cerebras agreed to establish a national-scale AI supercomputer in India .","root":"cerebras-uae"},{"id":"mubadala","name":"Mubadala Investment Company","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["AI and robotics investment opportunities","AI-enabled healthcare through the combination of Mubadala Health and G42 Healthcare"],"confidence":0.82,"coverage":0.727,"news":1,"voices":1,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"Mubadala is an Abu Dhabi sovereign investor and a majority owner of G42; one profile estimates its G42 stake at about 70% in mid-2022â€“2023, while Reuters also identifies Mubadala as a G42 investor.  AGBI reported that Mubadalaâ€™s group CEO said the fund was targeting opportunities in AI and robotics.  Mubadala holds 45% of M42, formed through the combination of Mubadala Health and G42 Healthcare.  The announced healthcare combination was intended to bring together Mubadala Healthâ€™s patient care and G42 Healthcareâ€™s medical and data-centric technologies.","root":"mubadala"},{"id":"adnoc","name":"Abu Dhabi National Oil Company (ADNOC)","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Deploying AI to improve efficiency and create value across ADNOC operations","Applying agentic AI and large language models across the upstream value chain","Using proprietary data and domain knowledge for workflows including seismic analysis, geological modeling, and real-time process monitoring"],"confidence":0.86,"coverage":0.818,"news":1,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"ADNOC is a state energy company headquartered in Abu Dhabi, and its AI strategy includes the ambition to become a highly AI-enabled energy company . ENERGYai combines large language model technology with agentic AI trained for upstream workflows, with applications including seismic analysis, geological modeling, and real-time process monitoring . AIQ announced a three-year, $340 million contract to deploy ENERGYai and related solutions across ADNOCâ€™s upstream operations . AIQ began as an ADNOCâ€“G42 joint venture, and the announced restructuring gives Presight a 51% stake while ADNOC retains 49%; ADNOC was also to receive 4% of Presight .","root":"adnoc"},{"id":"dff","name":"Dubai Future Foundation","type":"government","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Agentic AI for government services","Rapid prototyping and deployment of AI-powered government services","Simplifying customer journeys and improving public services","Quality and digital compliance in government AI services"],"confidence":0.82,"coverage":0.727,"news":2,"voices":1,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"Dubai Future Foundationâ€™s official site describes a workforce drawn from multiple disciplines and from around the world.  On 5 October 2026, DFF announced the Agentic AI for Government Services Accelerator under Dubai Future Accelerators; it is organized by the Dubai Centre for Artificial Intelligence, an initiative overseen by DFF, in collaboration with Digital Dubai and DESC.  The accelerator is intended to help Dubai Government entities rapidly prototype and deploy agentic-AI-powered services while maintaining quality and digital compliance; the seed facts report 33 entities and 300+ use cases.  Khalfan Belhoul is identified as DFFâ€™s chief executive, and is quoted describing AI as opening new horizons for governments to imagine future services.","root":"dff"},{"id":"dcai","name":"Dubai Centre for Artificial Intelligence","type":"government","hq":"Dubai","parent":"Dubai Future Foundation","focus":["Enabling government entities to develop agentic AI-powered services","Accelerating Dubaiâ€™s AI sector by recognising trusted AI companies through the Dubai AI Seal"],"confidence":0.76,"coverage":0.636,"news":3,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":4,"summary":"Dubai Centre for Artificial Intelligence (DCAI) is an initiative overseen by Dubai Future Foundation and organised the Agentic AI for Government Services Accelerator with Digital Dubai and the Dubai Electronic Security Center.  The programme is intended to help government entities develop agentic AI-powered services more quickly while maintaining quality and digital compliance.  Participating entities are to work with companies certified under the Dubai AI Seal, an initiative launched by DCAI to recognise trusted AI companies and support growth in Dubaiâ€™s AI sector.  An article dated 2026-06-02 reports that a DCAI study found 66% of Artificial Intelligence companies use Dubai as their global hub.","root":"dff"},{"id":"digital-dubai","name":"Digital Dubai","type":"government","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Agentic AI-powered government services","Digital government service development","Improving customer journeys and service quality","Digital compliance"],"confidence":0.78,"coverage":0.636,"news":1,"voices":1,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"The mission brief identifies Digital Dubai as the Dubai governmentâ€™s digital transformation authority.  Digital Dubai collaborated with the Dubai Centre for Artificial Intelligence and the Dubai Electronic Security Center on an accelerator intended to help government entities develop agentic AI-powered services more quickly while maintaining quality and digital compliance.  The accelerator was set to involve 33 government entities working with technology companies certified under the Dubai AI Seal.  Hamad Obaid Al Mansoori, Director General of Digital Dubai, said government service development is guided by the aim of improving peopleâ€™s experiences and anticipating evolving needs.","root":"digital-dubai"},{"id":"dge","name":"Department of Government Enablement (DGE), Abu Dhabi","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Government AI enablement","Ecosystem-wide collaboration across universities, technology companies, research institutes, investors, and startups","AI training for government employees through AiNative","Government AI work with Inception/G42"],"confidence":0.79,"coverage":0.727,"news":3,"voices":2,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"DGE is Abu Dhabiâ€™s government enablement department and, according to the supplied seed facts, works with Inception/G42 on government AI.  Director General Ruba Al Hassan has described Abu Dhabiâ€™s AI approach as an ecosystem effort involving universities, technology companies, research institutes, investors, and startups.  The National reported that DGE developed AiNative with OpenAI, Microsoft, and Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence, with a stated aim of providing training access to 20,000 government employees by the end of 2026.","root":"dge"},{"id":"dubai-ai-campus","name":"Dubai AI Campus","type":"government","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Artificial intelligence","Development and deployment of AI solutions","Collaboration among AI and technology companies"],"confidence":0.83,"coverage":0.545,"news":2,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"The Dubai AI Campus is located at the DIFC Innovation Hub and is described by DIFC as the regionâ€™s largest cluster for artificial intelligence and tech companies.  WAM reported that the campus cluster was inaugurated on 18 May 2024 by Sheikh Hamdan bin Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum.  CB Insights reports that the campus hosts over 200 AI companies and that 315 entities were under the Dubai AI Licence by mid-2026.","root":"dubai-ai-campus"},{"id":"doh-abu-dhabi","name":"Department of Health â€“ Abu Dhabi","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Artificial intelligence in healthcare delivery and clinical care","Population health intelligence and data-driven prevention","AI-enabled surgical care","Healthcare AI workforce capabilities and training","Patient safety and regulatory oversight of healthcare AI"],"confidence":0.84,"coverage":0.727,"news":2,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"DoH is described as Abu Dhabiâ€™s healthcare regulator and as encouraging healthcare AI while developing regulatory solutions focused on patient safety . The mission brief identifies a DoHâ€“Johnson & Johnson surgical network with Core42; the cited report says the network will use Johnson & Johnsonâ€™s Polyphonic digital ecosystem alongside AWS, NVIDIA, and Core42 technology . DoH partnered with MBZUAI and Core42 to launch the Global AI Healthcare Academy, with the stated aim of strengthening AI capabilities across the healthcare sector . DoH and Microsoft introduced an AI-powered Population Health Intelligence platform, while DoH leadership also linked an AI-powered diagnostic laboratory to Abu Dhabiâ€™s vision for smart, integrated healthcare .","root":"doh-abu-dhabi"},{"id":"dubai-police","name":"Dubai Police","type":"government","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Deepfake detection","AI and innovation","Autonomous security solutions co-created with Micropolis"],"confidence":0.48,"coverage":0.636,"news":1,"voices":3,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"The supplied seed facts record a Dubai Police deepfake warning dated 2026-10-10 that named the SARAAB detector and reported 91%; the metricâ€™s definition is not specified . Micropolis describes its work with the Dubai Police Innovation Lab as co-creation on autonomous security solutions . The available material does not verify Dubai Policeâ€™s website, founding year, leadership, or ownership details .","root":"dubai-police"},{"id":"camb-ai","name":"Camb.ai","type":"company","hq":"Dubai","parent":null,"focus":["Speech and dubbing AI","AI startup community member at DIFC / Dubai AI Campus"],"confidence":0.62,"coverage":0.364,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":7,"summary":"CAMB.AI is a speech and dubbing AI company and a Dubai AI Campus resident . Camb.ai is included among DIFC / Dubai AI Campus-based startups recognized in the Future 100 initiative . CB Insights lists CAMB.AI among major names at Dubai AI Campus, which it says hosts over 200 AI companies and had 315 registered entities under the Dubai AI Licence by mid-2026","root":"camb-ai"},{"id":"echotwin","name":"EchoTwin AI","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi (Hub71)","parent":null,"focus":["Transforms municipal fleets into mobile sensing networks and digital twins for infrastructure monitoring and predictive maintenance."],"confidence":0.72,"coverage":0.455,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"EchoTwin AI is identified as a Hub71 Cohort 18 company.  Its stated focus is transforming municipal fleets into mobile sensing networks and digital twins for infrastructure monitoring and predictive maintenance.  The available information does not verify a website, founding year, parent organization, ownership, or leadership.","root":"echotwin"},{"id":"neuphonic","name":"Neuphonic","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["On-device voice AI","Efficient voice models that run on any device","Real-time voice interactions at scale"],"confidence":0.72,"coverage":0.455,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":8,"summary":"Neuphonic is a voice AI company in Hub71 Cohort 18.  Its focus includes running efficient voice models on any device.  The company is also described as enabling real-time voice interactions at scale.","root":"neuphonic"},{"id":"endimension","name":"Endimension Technology","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi (Hub71)","parent":null,"focus":["AI-first radiology platform that automates abnormality detection, triage, and reporting"],"confidence":0.55,"coverage":0.545,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":5,"summary":"Endimension Technology is identified as a Hub71 Cohort 18 company in the Hub71 + Life Sciences track.  Its AI-first radiology platform automates abnormality detection, triage, and reporting.  Its headquarters are identified as Abu Dhabi (Hub71); further details on its founding, ownership, leadership, and website are unavailable.","root":"endimension"},{"id":"steerai","name":"SteerAI","type":"company","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Off-road autonomous vehicle software","Ground unmanned ground vehicles (UGVs)","AI software for autonomous logistics, including navigation, fleet management and safety"],"confidence":0.78,"coverage":0.636,"news":1,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"SteerAI is an external partner focused on off-road autonomous vehicles and ground UGVs.  In January 2026, SteerAI partnered with EDGE, TII and Micropolis to deploy an advanced autonomous logistics platform.  The platform uses AI software for navigation, fleet management and safety.","root":"steerai"},{"id":"aiatc","name":"Artificial Intelligence and Advanced Technology Council","type":"government","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":null,"focus":["Artificial intelligence policy","Advanced technology policy"],"confidence":0.55,"coverage":0.455,"news":0,"voices":1,"models":0,"unavailable":8,"summary":"AIATC is an Abu Dhabi council for AI and advanced technology policy.  Gulf News identifies Khaldoon Khalifa Al Mubarak as the councilâ€™s secretary general.  In reporting on G42â€™s U.S. approval for advanced AI chip exports, Al Mubarak described the decision as affirming trust in the UAEâ€“U.S. relationship and a shared strategic outlook.","root":"aiatc"},{"id":"injazat","name":"Injazat","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"Core42","focus":["Enterprise cloud and AI capabilities through its merger into Core42"],"confidence":0.78,"coverage":0.636,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":6,"summary":"Injazat merged into Core42 in October 2023 and is tracked here for lineage only, excluded from aggregates . Core42 was formed by merging G42 Cloud, Inception, and Injazat, and was described as a platform for enterprise cloud and AI capabilities . Core42 is identified as a G42 subsidiary, while separate ownership details for Injazat are unavailable .","root":"g42"},{"id":"aspire","name":"ASPIRE","type":"subsidiary","hq":"Abu Dhabi","parent":"Advanced Technology Research Council","focus":["Technology programme management"],"confidence":0.55,"coverage":0.364,"news":0,"voices":0,"models":0,"unavailable":9,"summary":"ASPIRE is identified as a subsidiary headquartered in Abu Dhabi.  It is identified as part of ATRC.  ASPIRE is described as ATRCâ€™s technology programme management pillar.","root":"atrc"}],"rootNames":{"ai-data-authority":"Artificial Intelligence and Data Authority","g42":"G42","space42":"Space42 PLC","mgx":"MGX","atrc":"Advanced Technology Research Council","edge":"EDGE Group","mbzuai":"Mohamed bin Zayed University of Artificial Intelligence","khalifa-university":"Khalifa University of Science and Technology","airev":"AIREV","eand-enterprise":"e& enterprise","hub71":"Hub71","micropolis":"Micropolis Robotics","xpanceo":"XPANCEO","derq":"Derq","astra-tech":"Astra Tech","saal-ai":"Saal.ai","purehealth":"PureHealth","cntxt":"CNTXT AI","positron":"Positron AI Ltd","cerebras-uae":"Cerebras Systems","mubadala":"Mubadala Investment Company","adnoc":"Abu Dhabi National Oil Company (ADNOC)","dff":"Dubai Future Foundation","digital-dubai":"Digital Dubai","dge":"Department of Government Enablement (DGE), Abu Dhabi","dubai-ai-campus":"Dubai AI Campus","doh-abu-dhabi":"Department of Health â€“ Abu Dhabi","dubai-police":"Dubai Police","camb-ai":"Camb.ai","echotwin":"EchoTwin AI","neuphonic":"Neuphonic","endimension":"Endimension Technology","steerai":"SteerAI","aiatc":"Artificial Intelligence and Advanced Technology Council"}}]],null,"$L21"]}]
